# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository, and check them out as LF on
# every platform — including Windows, where Git's default core.autocrlf=true
# would otherwise convert them on checkout.
#
# This is not a style preference, it is load-bearing:
# test/securityHeaders.test.js reads index.html off disk, sha256s the raw bytes
# of its inline theme <script>, and asserts the digest matches the hash pinned
# in vercel.json's Content-Security-Policy. CRLF changes those bytes, so a
# Windows clone with the default settings fails that test with a hash mismatch
# that reads like a broken CSP rather than a line-ending problem. The test is
# right to hash raw bytes — it guards what Vite actually ships — so the fix
# belongs here.
#
# Every tracked file was LF when this landed, so this changes no content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
